iption":"Amusing health propaganda trailer on the dangers of sneezing. NHS in 1948. Public health. Colds. Coughs and Sneezes spread diseases, Modern Public Health Campaign Films. Post War era.","date":"1945","year":"1945","subject":"health; colds; nhs","pick":"1","hidden":"true","publicdate":"2005-10-10 00:10:11","addeddate":"2005-10-10 07:09:59","uploader":"florian@archive.org","updater":["nVIR","ewingrr"],"updatedate":["2005-10-10 00:12:57","2006-10-23 18:34:53"],"sponsor":"Ministry of Information for Ministry of Health","director":"Richard Massingham","publisher":"Public Relationship Films","sound":"sound","color":"color","runtime":"1:25","credits":"Public Information Films","rights":"UK Crown Copyright","language":"english","coverage":"Great Britain","backup_location":"ia903600_10","ia_orig__runtime":"1 Minute 25 Seconds"},"reviews":[{"reviewbody":"I've seen this a few times on TV, it's great to have stuff like this on the archive.\n\nAfter some of semi-relevant slapstick, we are treated to my personal favourite public information film star spreading disease and pestilence to his fellow men via the most implausible-sounding sneezes ever recorded, \"WHOOOF! WHOOF! WHOOF!\".\n\nThen, the stern and very 1940s narrator grabs the man and sits him down for a lesson in the correct employment of a handkerchief.\n\nThis man's dopey facial expression is priceless, and the film is well worth watching just for that and the WHOOF sound effect.\n\nSee also the follow-up on how to clean your hankie at http://www.archive.org/details/dont_spread_germs_TNA","reviewtitle":"Classic public information film","stars":"5","reviewer":"boffy_b","createdate":"2005-11-05 16:52:48","reviewdate":"2005-11-05 16:52:48"},{"reviewbody":"The hero of this film can't muster a sneeze when required, so the narrator's arm comes into the frame and shakes a substantial amount of pepper all over the poor fellow's head.  \n\nNO, really, a LOT of pepper -- like three or four cups.","reviewtitle":"Sadistic Narrator","stars":"4","reviewer":"ridetheory","createdate":"2006-12-17 07:11:44","reviewdate":"2006-12-17 07:11:44"},{"reviewbody":"...especially all the sneezing noises at the end.","reviewtitle":"funny, but gets redundant...","reviewer":"elocina","reviewdate":"2007-03-23 18:26:33","createdate":"2007-03-23 18:26:33","stars":"4"},{"reviewbody":"i\u00b4ve learned a lot in this nice short movie!","reviewtitle":"gesundheit!","reviewer":"Ardath Bey","reviewdate":"2007-09-09 02:03:30","createdate":"2007-09-09 02:03:30","stars":"5"},{"reviewbody":"But I marvel at how that man sneezes *exactly* the same way, same pitch, every time! ","reviewtitle":"Hilarious","reviewer":"RetroXana","reviewdate":"2008-09-26 19:38:32","createdate":"2008-09-26 19:38:32","stars":"4"},{"reviewtitle":"Ever Hear of A Mask?","reviewbody":"People walk around wearing them all the time.  Just saw a couple in Walmart today wearing masks.  It's October, the kiddies are back in school spreading everything around, so why not? I thought.  That old Brit did a good sneeze act.  \n\nI remember when Brits looked like that.","stars":"0","reviewer":"JSBejma","reviewdate":"2022-10-27 04:16:44","createdate":"2022-10-27 04:16:44","reviewer_itemname":"@jsbejma"}],"server":"dn601201.us.archive.org","simplelists":{"solo_manifest":{"solo_manifest_dn601201":{"sys_changed_by":{"source":"task","task_id":"5445338165"},"sys_last_changed":"2026-06-17 04:37:34.004651"}}},"solo":true,"uniq":1071378027,"workable_servers":["dn601201.us.archive.org"]}